          "main": [
            "This version is the instrument panel: GitHub Pages sends a visitor signal to Vercel, Vercel dispatches GitHub Actions, and the site records a new contributor version.",
            "The page stays mostly white so the mechanism is visible. The weird part is not decoration; it is the page teaching itself to listen."
          ],
          "quote": "A website that can receive a signal should show the wire."
        },
        "about": {
          "title": "About the loop",
          "time": "Signal version",
          "paragraphs": [
            "This branch of the site exists to make the feedback system legible: a handle, a request, a dispatch, a merge, and a new version in the dial.",
            "Automerge still keeps a local thread of the visitor state, while the canonical public lineage lives in JSON that GitHub Pages can serve."
          ],
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/Hieronymus_Bosch_013.jpg/960px-Hieronymus_Bosch_013.jpg",
